        "original_id": "18c2376f-5a78-5247-8442-09acc8b4107e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Kingsford Smith, Charles Ulm\n- Companies: Australian National Airways\n- Products: Southern Cloud, Avro 618 Ten\n- Places: Australia, United States\n- Topics: trans-Pacific flight, Australian airline services\n\nFacts:\n- In 1928, Charles Kingsford Smith earned global fame by making the first trans-Pacific flight from the United States to Australia.\n- In 1929, Charles Kingsford Smith and Charles Ulm founded Australian National Airways.\n- Australian National Airways was a short-lived Australian airline.\n- In the early 1930s, Australian National Airways operated five Avro 618 Ten three-engined aircraft on daily airline services between several Australian cities.\n- The Southern Cloud, registered VH-UMF, was one of the five Avro 618 Ten aircraft operated by Australian National Airways.",
